AUDIO: 'In this video, we\'re going to do a Hollywood VFX style battle with C Dance 2 versus Gemini Omni. Okay, let\'s get into it. I\'ve been doing tons of testing with C Dance 2 and Gemini Omni to try and recreate some Hollywood VFX shots.'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And I\'ve been really surprised with how far you can push these models. I\'ve also created a free prompts document containing some of the prompts from this video. If you do want to recreate some of these shots. I\'ve been doing all of'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'my testing for these shots inside of Open Art. I\'ll just give you a quick rundown on the settings here. As you can see on the homepage, they have this director mode, which is pretty new. Now, I\'ll show you some of my testing using director mode later on and it is very,'

[00:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'very impressive. Most of the VFX shots that I\'ve made are using reference footage of myself as I wanted to see how well C Dance 2 and Gemini Omni can alter my footage to fit the effects that I\'m looking for. So, to use these models in'

[00:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Open Art, we go to the video tab and I\'ve got C Dance 2 selected here. Now, you can do these effects with just a starting image and a prompt, but for most of my VFX shots, I\'m actually adding the effects to reference footage'

[01:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of myself. So, to do that, you go to text with reference and if you click here, you can choose to upload images, video, and audio. Now, a difference with C Dance 2 and Gemini Omni is that with C Dance 2, you can have a max of 15'

[01:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'seconds, whereas Gemini Omni has a maximum of 10 seconds. Another huge difference is that C Dance 2 has a max resolution of 4K, whereas Gemini Omni only tops out at 720p. But, the great thing about Gemini Omni is that it is a'

[01:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'lot cheaper in credits. Now, you can select Gemini Omni flash from the video models here, but within this video mode here, you can only upload images at the moment. So, to upload videos in Gemini Omni, we go to all tools and then edit'

[01:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'video. Then, from here, you can upload your video and add the prompt on what you want to happen in the video. So, I\'ll start off on this superhero shot. I wanted to recreate some of the shots in the latest Spider-Man trailer. Now,'

[01:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'these kind of shots are a bit more subtle and cinematic rather than me swinging through a city as it would have been quite hard to get the reference footage for that one. So in the trailer they\'ve got that shot of Spider-Man sitting upside down on a metal beam. So'

[02:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I tried my best to kind of replicate that shot. So I just uploaded that footage into Gemini Omni and gave it this prompt. So as you can see in the prompt I say keep the performance and camera motion from my reference video. Then I explain what should happen in the'

[02:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'video and I think it looks pretty good. I think because using the footage and a text prompt it did a really good job at kind of following that motion really well and making a pretty cool looking shot. Now I found because Gemini Omni is'

[02:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'only 720p when you kind of blow the image up it does look a lot more AI and kind of video gamey. Now jumping over to SeaArt 2 the problem I had here is you\'re not allowed to use any'

[02:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'superheroes so I had to kind of make my own suit. So jumping over to image you can select your image model here. I just used Nano Banana 2 and I just prompted it with spandex superhero suit with full'

[02:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'head mask on white background and it gave me this pretty generic looking superhero suit. I also generated this image in Nano Banana 2. Then when uploading both of those reference images with this prompt it generated this'

[03:09] [scene:talk]
